The code filters out examples/collocations that don't contain the exact word, but **does not validate** whether the filtering resulted in empty arrays. If the AI returns synonyms or related words instead of the exact target word, all examples get filtered out, and the service returns `exampleSentences: []` and `commonCollocations: []` **without raising an error**.

The same silent filtering happens in the Ollama/Cloud paths via `OllamaWordExplanationResponse.toResult(filteringFor:)` at lines 1536-1537, which also lacks post-filtering validation.

