3. **SwiftUI Behavior**: In SwiftUI, when you pass a String literal to `.confirmationDialog()`, it is **automatically treated as a LocalizedStringKey**. This is the standard, documented design. The framework will automatically look up the string in Localizable.xcstrings.

### Why the Claim is Incorrect

The suggestion to change it to `.confirmationDialog(Text("Clear all translation history?"), ...)` is **not valid**. The `confirmationDialog()` modifier's title parameter is designed to accept String literals as localization keys—this is the recommended pattern in SwiftUI, not an error.

**Conclusion**: The code is already correct and properly localized. No changes are needed.

